ndividual, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "22 – 23 July 1980"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/583"} "Futbolny polya, Legkoatletichesky futbolny kompleks, Moskva"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/103487"} "37 from 16 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "After winning the world title in 1977 and 1979 " [:a {:href "/athletes/23596"} "Aleksandr Romankov"] " of the USSR had every right to be considered favourite for the Olympic title. His title hopes was increased when 1976 Olympic champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/22653"} "Fabio Dal Zotto"] " withdrew himself from consideration for a place on the Italian team.\nRomankov would have won the Olympic title had he beaten teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/23606"} "Volodymyr Smyrnov"] " in the final pool but a defeat forced him into a three-way barrage with Smyrnov and Frenchman " [:a {:href "/athletes/21905"} "Pascal Jolyot"] ", the reigning World silver medallist.\nSmyrnov beat Jolyot with ease but then Jolyot scored an equally decisive win over Romankov.  Smyrnov then defeated Romankov in a close fought match to claim the title.\n" [:a {:href "/athletes/23606"} "Volodymyr Smyrnov"] "’s life ended in tragic circumstances. He was competing at the 1982 World Championships when his opponent’s weapon broke, pierced his mask and went into his brain.\nHe died a few days later."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "138"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/23606"} "Vladimir Smirnov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} [:span